<title>MEXICO: Pemex details increased crude, natgas production.</title>
<headline>Pemex details increased crude, natgas production.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1996-12-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexican state-owned oil and gas monopoly Petroleos Mexicanos (Pemex) said Tuesday it increased crude production by 9.5 percent from January to November compared with the same period in 1995 to an average 2.854 million barrels per day (bpd).</p>
<p>The company said natural gas production in the same period rose 12.4 percent from 1995, to an average 4.19 billion cubic feet per day (cfd).</p>
